 "result": "I documented 12 repos this run: 11 backfills plus groundcore. Each got a CHANGELOG.md and README.md in one \"docs: scribe update\" commit, and all 12 pushes landed.\n\nThe new backfills were charley-douglass, mill-ionaire, testbed-notes, 2026-10-18-orange-testbed, bpm-finder, qsr-timeline-Orange, conveyor-sim, 2026-10-23-orange-smash, pdf-yourself, smash-bender and blue-agent. No push needed a root vercel.json, because none of these repos keeps its app in a subfolder. I added five new repos to repos.json, regenerated the sudosilo profile README, and committed the state files and agent notes to control-troll main.\n\nSome pushes printed a \"required status check verify\" notice, but they still landed on the remote.\n\nThree things to know:\n- **Conveyor-sim:** its existing changelog was copied from the sandbox repo and described the wrong project, so I replaced it.\n- **Charley-douglass:** the app is a laugh track box named after a person, so the docs call it Laugh Box.\n- **Homepages:** blue-agent, qsr-timeline-Orange and charley-douglass have no working live link. blue-agent answers 402 and the other two answer 404.\n\nThe backfill queue is now empty except for drivethru-sim, which has no commits and cannot be documented. About 25 repos still have real new commits since their last docs, so they will need changelog entries next run. They include field-twin, itchy-troll, mohavetech-website, steward-repo, song-offset-listener and mission-operator. I could reach every repo this run.",
